From 41ee373df2684b72cf42f6f588dc227db4659e6f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: neolink-addon <neolink-addon@localhost>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 11:05:56 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 27/27] core: an unreadable XML payload no longer drops the
 connection

The Argus MagiCam answers PushInfo (124) with a payload that does not
decrypt to XML. The parse error dropped the whole connection, and the
push registration, retried after every reconnect, then cut every live
view off (reconnecting every 1-3 s, no frame ever reached the client).
The message is complete at that point (its length is in the header), so
log a warning and deliver it without a payload; callers still get the
response code.
---
 Cargo.lock               | Bin 124106 -> 123974 bytes
 crates/core/src/bc/de.rs |  39 ++++++++++++++++++++++++---------------
 2 files changed, 24 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Cargo.lock b/Cargo.lock
index 376edaa235633df1d0b9e03833dcb97ae1d0b137..7efe0a7988f8c72d6ae0d189feba7c3c2cb2f67e 100644
GIT binary patch
